§§ `Order 44 Rule 3 -- a person under disability must sue, etc., by litigation representative`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 3(1): "A person under disability may not bring, make a claim in, defend, make a counterclaim in, or intervene in any proceedings, or appear in any proceedings under a judgment or order notice of which has been served on him or her, except by his or her litigation representative."
-- FORK QA | the person acts by the litigation representative: NOTHING (a lifted bar grants nothing) | JUST TRUE (the exception permits it)
-- src:5983 | 3. —(1) A person under disability may not bring, make a claim in, defend, make a counterclaim in, or intervene in any proceedings, or appear in any proceedings under a judgment or order notice of which has been served on him or her, except by his or her litigation representative. (2) Subject to these Rules, anything which in the ordinary conduct of any proceedings is required or authorised by a provision of these Rules to be done by a party to the proceedings must or may, if the party is a person under disability, be done by his or her litigation representative.
@ref O 44 r 3(1) (src:5983)
GIVEN `the person is a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the step is to bring, make a claim in, defend, make a counterclaim in, or intervene in proceedings, or to appear in proceedings under a judgment or order notice of which has been served on the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts by the person's litigation representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 3(1) the person under disability may take the step` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the person is a person under disability`) OR (NOT `the step is to bring, make a claim in, defend, make a counterclaim in, or intervene in proceedings, or to appear in proceedings under a judgment or order notice of which has been served on the person`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A person under disability may not bring, make a claim in, defend, make a counterclaim in, or intervene in any proceedings, or appear in any proceedings under a judgment or order notice of which has been served on him or her"
           IF `the person acts by the person's litigation representative`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except by his or her litigation representative" -- the bar is lifted and grants nothing (QA)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person under disability may not ... except by his or her litigation representative"

-- Rule 3(2): "Subject to these Rules, anything which in the ordinary conduct of any proceedings is required or authorised by a provision of these Rules to be done by a party to the proceedings must or may, if the party is a person under disability, be done by his or her litigation representative."
