-- Rule 4(5): "Except where the litigation representative of a person under disability has been appointed by the Court — (a) the name of any person must not be used in a cause or matter as litigation representative of a person
-- under disability; (b) a notice of intention to contest or not contest must not be filed in a cause or matter for a person under disability; and (c) a person under disability is not entitled to appear by his or her litigation
-- representative on the hearing of a summons which has been served on him or her, until the documents listed in paragraph (6) have been filed in the Registry."
-- The "until" bar (ruling (d)): a twin says whether the bar applies; the bar itself is JUST TRUE before the documents are filed and JUST FALSE after.
DECLARE `o 44 r 4(5) the step` IS ONE OF
    `o 44 r 4(5)(a) use the name of a person as litigation representative of the person under disability`
    `o 44 r 4(5)(b) file a notice of intention to contest or not contest for the person under disability`
    `o 44 r 4(5)(c) appear by the litigation representative on the hearing of a summons served on the person under disability`
    `o 44 r 4(5) some other step`

