-- Rule 4(6): "The documents referred to in paragraph (5) are the following: (a) a written consent in Form 73 to be litigation representative ... given by the person proposing to be such litigation representative; (b) where the person proposing ..., being a person lacking capacity [sic], is authorised under the Act to conduct the proceedings ... a copy, sealed with the seal of the Court, of the order or other authorisation ...; (c) except where the person proposing ... is authorised as mentioned in sub-paragraph (b), a certificate in Form 74 made by the solicitor for the person under disability certifying (i) ... (ii) ... (iii) ..."
-- The text says "the person proposing to be such litigation representative ..., being a person lacking capacity" in (b) and (c); the states of the documents below are given by the asker, and the functions that decide which documents are required follow fork F44.4.
DECLARE `o 44 r 4(6) a document is required` IS ONE OF
    `o 44 r 4(6) it is filed`
    `o 44 r 4(6) it is not filed`
    `o 44 r 4(6) it is not required on these facts`

