-- Rule 4(6)(b) and (c), which documents are REQUIRED, decided from two facts: whether the person under disability is a person lacking capacity, and whether the person proposing to be litigation representative is authorised under the Act.
-- FORK F44.4 | "the person proposing to be such litigation representative of the person under disability, being a person lacking capacity, is authorised under the Act to conduct the proceedings ... in the name of the person lacking capacity": "being a person lacking capacity" attaches to the person under disability (the person in whose name the authorisation conducts the proceedings), so an authorised deputy who has capacity brings (b) into play and takes (c) away | it attaches to the proposer as printed, so (b) and (c) turn on the proposer lacking capacity
-- (b) lists the sealed copy "where the person proposing ..., being a person lacking capacity, is authorised under the Act"; (c) lists the Form 74 certificate "except where" that person is so authorised.
-- Both are lists of documents, so a document that is not listed on these facts is the text's own no (the QD pattern above).
