-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 44 Rule 5 -- appointment where no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 5(1): "Where — (a) in an action against a person under disability begun by originating claim, or by originating application, no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed in the originating claim action
-- for that person; or (b) the defendant to an action serves a defence and counterclaim on a person under disability who is not already a party to the action, and no notice ... is filed for that person, an application for the
-- appointment by the Court of a litigation representative of that person must be made by the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) after the time limited (as respects that person) for filing and serving a notice ... and
-- before proceeding further with the action or counterclaim."
-- The "after the time limited" and "before proceeding further" limits are each yes/no inputs: the day on which the time limited expires is Order 3's.
-- src:6008 | 5. —(1) Where — ( a )
-- src:6009 | in an action against a person under disability begun by originating claim, or by originating application, no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed in the originating claim action for that person; or
-- src:6010 | ( b )
-- src:6011 | the defendant to an action serves a defence and counterclaim on a person under disability who is not already a party to the action, and no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed for that person,
-- src:6012 | an application for the appointment by the Court of a litigation representative of that person must be made by the claimant or defendant (as the case may be) after the time limited (as respects that person) for filing and serving a notice of intention to contest or not contest and before proceeding further with the action or counterclaim.
@ref O 44 r 5(1) (src:6008-6012)
GIVEN `in an action against a person under disability begun by originating claim or by originating application, no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed for that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defendant to an action serves a defence and counterclaim on a person under disability who is not already a party to the action, and no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed for that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 5(1) the duty to apply for the appointment of a litigation representative arises` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT ((`in an action against a person under disability begun by originating claim or by originating application, no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed for that person` OR `the defendant to an action serves a defence and counterclaim on a person under disability who is not already a party to the action, and no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed for that person`)))
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in an action against a person under disability no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed for that person, or the defendant serves a defence and counterclaim on a person under disability who is not already a party and no notice is filed for that person, an application for the appointment by the Court of a litigation representative of that person must be made" (the condition is not met)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

