           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where in an action against a person under disability no notice of intention to contest or not contest is filed for that person, or the defendant serves a defence and counterclaim on a person under disability who is not already a party and no notice is filed for that person, an application for the appointment by the Court of a litigation representative of that person must be made" -- the duty does not arise (QD); `o 44 r 5(1) the duty to apply for the appointment of a litigation representative arises` answers JUST FALSE
