-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 44 Rule 6 -- application to discharge or vary certain orders`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 6: "An application to the Court on behalf of a person under disability served with an order made without notice under Order 4, Rule 5 for the discharge or variation of the order must be made —
-- (a) if a litigation representative is acting for that person in the cause or matter in which the order is made, within 14 days after the service of the order on that person; or (b) if there is no litigation
-- representative acting for that person in that cause or matter, within 14 days after the appointment of such a litigation representative to act for him or her."
-- src:6027 | 6. An application to the Court on behalf of a person under disability served with an order made without notice under Order 4, Rule 5 for the discharge or variation of the order must be made — ( a )
-- src:6028 | if a litigation representative is acting for that person in the cause or matter in which the order is made, within 14 days after the service of the order on that person; or
-- src:6029 | ( b )
-- src:6030 | if there is no litigation representative acting for that person in that cause or matter, within 14 days after the appointment of such a litigation representative to act for him or her.
@ref O 44 r 6 (src:6027-6030)
`o 44 r 6 the period for the application` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

DECLARE `o 44 r 6 the event the 14 days run from` IS ONE OF
    `o 44 r 6(a) the service of the order on the person under disability`
    `o 44 r 6(b) the appointment of a litigation representative to act for the person under disability`

-- src:6027 | 6. An application to the Court on behalf of a person under disability served with an order made without notice under Order 4, Rule 5 for the discharge or variation of the order must be made — ( a )
-- src:6028 | if a litigation representative is acting for that person in the cause or matter in which the order is made, within 14 days after the service of the order on that person; or
-- src:6029 | ( b )
-- src:6030 | if there is no litigation representative acting for that person in that cause or matter, within 14 days after the appointment of such a litigation representative to act for him or her.
@ref O 44 r 6 (src:6027-6030)
GIVEN `a litigation representative is acting for that person in the cause or matter in which the order is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `o 44 r 6 the event the 14 days run from`
`o 44 r 6 the event from which the period for the application runs` MEANS
    IF `a litigation representative is acting for that person in the cause or matter in which the order is made`
    THEN `o 44 r 6(a) the service of the order on the person under disability`
    ELSE `o 44 r 6(b) the appointment of a litigation representative to act for the person under disability`

-- The last day (Order 3, Rule 3) is counted from the event that `o 44 r 6 the event from which the period for the application runs` names.
-- src:6027 | 6. An application to the Court on behalf of a person under disability served with an order made without notice under Order 4, Rule 5 for the discharge or variation of the order must be made — ( a )
