@ref O 44 r 6 (src:6027-6030)
GIVEN `the application is on behalf of a person under disability served with an order made without notice under Order 4, Rule 5 for the discharge or variation of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made on the day` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 6 the application is made in time` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `the application is on behalf of a person under disability served with an order made without notice under Order 4, Rule 5 for the discharge or variation of the order`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application to the Court on behalf of a person under disability served with an order made without notice under Order 4, Rule 5"
           IF `the application is made on the day` GREATER THAN `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act`
