§§ `Order 44 Rule 11 -- control of money recovered by a person under disability`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 11(1): "Where in any proceedings (a) money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability; or (b) money paid into Court is accepted
-- by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability, the money must be dealt with in accordance with directions given by the Court."
-- The part roc2 (Order 14, Rule 3(6)) points here: `o 44 r 11(1) the duty to deal with the money as the Court directs arises` is what it should ask.
-- src:6045 | 11. —(1) Where in any proceedings — ( a )
-- src:6046 | money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability; or
-- src:6047 | ( b )
-- src:6048 | money paid into Court is accepted by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability,
-- src:6049 | the money must be dealt with in accordance with directions given by the Court.
@ref O 44 r 11(1) (src:6045-6049)
GIVEN `money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `money paid into Court is accepted by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 11(1) the duty to deal with the money as the Court directs arises` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT ((`money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability` OR `money paid into Court is accepted by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability`)))
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any proceedings money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability, or money paid into Court is accepted by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability, the money must be dealt with in accordance with directions given by the Court" (the condition is not met)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- FORK QB | bare "must" (Where in any proceedings money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability, or money paid into Court is accepted by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability, the money must be dealt with in accordance with directions given by the Court): the requirement is not met | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- FORK QD | the duty does not arise (the "where", "before" or "unless" is unmet): NOTHING, with the companion `o 44 r 11(1) the duty to deal with the money as the Court directs arises` answering JUST FALSE | JUST TRUE ("nothing is unmet")
-- src:6045 | 11. —(1) Where in any proceedings — ( a )
-- src:6046 | money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability; or
-- src:6047 | ( b )
-- src:6048 | money paid into Court is accepted by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability,
-- src:6049 | the money must be dealt with in accordance with directions given by the Court.
@ref O 44 r 11(1) (src:6045-6049)
GIVEN `money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `money paid into Court is accepted by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money is dealt with in accordance with directions given by the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 11(1) the money is dealt with in accordance with directions given by the Court` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT ((`money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability` OR `money paid into Court is accepted by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability`)))
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where in any proceedings money is recovered by or on behalf of, or adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid to, or for the benefit of, a person under disability, or money paid into Court is accepted by or on behalf of a claimant who is a person under disability, the money must be dealt with in accordance with directions given by the Court" -- the duty does not arise (QD); `o 44 r 11(1) the duty to deal with the money as the Court directs arises` answers JUST FALSE
           IF `the money is dealt with in accordance with directions given by the Court`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); O 44 r 11(1) does not say what follows when a requirement is not met


-- src:6050 | (2) Directions given under this Rule may provide that the money must, as to the whole or any part of the money, be paid into Court and invested or otherwise dealt with.
@ref O 44 r 11(2) (src:6050)
GIVEN `the directions are given under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 11(2) the directions may provide that the money be paid into Court and invested or otherwise dealt with` MEANS
    IF `the directions are given under this Rule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Directions given under this Rule"

-- Rule 11(3): "Without affecting paragraphs (1) and (2), directions given under this Rule may include any general or special directions that the Court thinks fit to give and, in particular, directions (a) as to how the money
-- is to be applied or dealt with; and (b) as to any payment to be made ... to the claimant, or to the litigation representative in respect of moneys paid or expenses incurred ... or to the claimant's solicitor in respect of costs."
-- "in particular" illustrates the general power; the list does not limit it.
-- src:6051 | (3) Without affecting paragraphs (1) and (2), directions given under this Rule may include any general or special directions that the Court thinks fit to give and, in particular, directions — ( a )
-- src:6052 | as to how the money is to be applied or dealt with; and
-- src:6053 | ( b )
-- src:6054 | as to any payment to be made, either directly or out of the amount paid into Court, to the claimant, or to the litigation representative in respect of moneys paid or expenses incurred for or on behalf or for the benefit of the person under disability or for his or her maintenance or otherwise for his or her benefit or to the claimant’s solicitor in respect of costs.
@ref O 44 r 11(3) (src:6051-6054)
GIVEN `the directions are given under this Rule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 11(3) the directions may include the direction` MEANS
    IF `the directions are given under this Rule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "directions given under this Rule may include any general or special directions that the Court thinks fit to give"

-- Rule 11(4): "Where pursuant to directions given under this Rule money is paid into Court to be invested or otherwise dealt with, the money (including any interest on such money) may not be paid out, nor may any securities
-- in which the money is invested, or the dividends on such securities, be sold, transferred or paid out of Court, except in accordance with an order of the Court."
-- FORK QA | the step is in accordance with an order of the Court: NOTHING (a lifted bar grants nothing) | JUST TRUE (the exception permits it)
-- src:6055 | (4) Where pursuant to directions given under this Rule money is paid into Court to be invested or otherwise dealt with, the money (including any interest on such money) may not be paid out, nor may any securities in which the money is invested, or the dividends on such securities, be sold, transferred or paid out of Court, except in accordance with an order of the Court.
@ref O 44 r 11(4) (src:6055)
GIVEN `pursuant to directions given under this Rule money is paid into Court to be invested or otherwise dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the step is to pay out the money (including interest), or to sell, transfer or pay out of Court the securities in which it is invested or the dividends on them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the step is in accordance with an order of the Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 11(4) the step may be taken` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `pursuant to directions given under this Rule money is paid into Court to be invested or otherwise dealt with`) OR (NOT `the step is to pay out the money (including interest), or to sell, transfer or pay out of Court the securities in which it is invested or the dividends on them`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where pursuant to directions given under this Rule money is paid into Court to be invested or otherwise dealt with, the money (including any interest on such money) may not be paid out, nor may any securities ... be sold, transferred or paid out of Court"
           IF `the step is in accordance with an order of the Court`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "except in accordance with an order of the Court" -- the bar is lifted and grants nothing (QA)
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not be paid out ... except in accordance with an order of the Court"

-- Rule 11(5): "Paragraphs (1) to (4) apply in relation to a counterclaim by or on behalf of a person under disability, and a claim made by or on behalf of such a person in an action by any other person for relief under
-- Order 33, Rule 36, as if for references to a claimant there were substituted references to a defendant."
-- src:6056 | (5) Paragraphs (1) to (4) apply in relation to a counterclaim by or on behalf of a person under disability, and a claim made by or on behalf of such a person in an action by any other person for relief under Order 33, Rule 36, as if for references to a claimant there were substituted references to a defendant.
@ref O 44 r 11(5) (src:6056)
GIVEN `it is a counterclaim by or on behalf of a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a claim made by or on behalf of a person under disability in an action by any other person for relief under Order 33, Rule 36` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 11(5) paragraphs (1) to (4) apply with the claimant read as the defendant` MEANS
    IF `it is a counterclaim by or on behalf of a person under disability` OR `it is a claim made by or on behalf of a person under disability in an action by any other person for relief under Order 33, Rule 36`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a counterclaim by or on behalf of a person under disability, and a claim made by or on behalf of such a person in an action by any other person for relief under Order 33, Rule 36"

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 44 Rule 12 -- apportionment under the Civil Law Act`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 12(1): "Where a single sum of money is paid into Court under Order 14, Rule 1, in satisfaction of causes of action arising under the Civil Law Act and that sum is accepted, the money must be apportioned between the
-- different causes of action by the Court either when giving directions for dealing with it under Rule 13 (if that Rule applies) or when authorising its payment out of Court."
-- The text says "under Rule 13 (if that Rule applies)"; Rule 13 is about service on a person under disability.  The reference is followed as printed.
-- src:6058 | 12. —(1) Where a single sum of money is paid into Court under Order 14, Rule 1, in satisfaction of causes of action arising under the Civil Law Act and that sum is accepted, the money must be apportioned between the different causes of action by the Court either when giving directions for dealing with it under Rule 13 (if that Rule applies) or when authorising its payment out of Court. (2) Where, in an action in which a claim under the Civil Law Act is made by or on behalf of more than one person, a sum in respect of damages is adjudged or ordered or agreed to be paid in satisfaction of the claim, or a sum of money paid into Court under Order 14, Rule 1, is accepted in satisfaction of the cause of action under the Civil Law Act, it must be apportioned between those persons by the Court.
@ref O 44 r 12(1) (src:6058)
GIVEN `a single sum of money is paid into Court under Order 14, Rule 1, in satisfaction of causes of action arising under the Civil Law Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that sum is accepted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 12(1) the duty to apportion the money arises` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`a single sum of money is paid into Court under Order 14, Rule 1, in satisfaction of causes of action arising under the Civil Law Act` AND `that sum is accepted`))
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a single sum of money is paid into Court under Order 14, Rule 1, in satisfaction of causes of action arising under the Civil Law Act and that sum is accepted, the money must be apportioned between the different causes of action by the Court" (the condition is not met)
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- FORK QB | bare "must" (Where a single sum of money is paid into Court under Order 14, Rule 1, in satisfaction of causes of action arising under the Civil Law Act and that sum is accepted, the money must be apportioned between the different causes of action by the Court): the requirement is not met | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- FORK QD | the duty does not arise (the "where", "before" or "unless" is unmet): NOTHING, with the companion `o 44 r 12(1) the duty to apportion the money arises` answering JUST FALSE | JUST TRUE ("nothing is unmet")
