-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Order 44 Rule 13 -- service of certain documents on a person under disability`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- Rule 13(1): "Where in any proceedings a document is required to be served personally on any person and that person is a person under disability, this Rule applies."
-- src:6061 | 13. —(1) Where in any proceedings a document is required to be served personally on any person and that person is a person under disability, this Rule applies. (2) Subject to this Rule and to Order 11, Rule 7( c ), the document must be served — ( a )
@ref O 44 r 13(1) (src:6061)
GIVEN `a document is required to be served personally on the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 13(1) this Rule applies` MEANS
    IF `a document is required to be served personally on the person` AND `the person is a person under disability`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in any proceedings a document is required to be served personally on any person and that person is a person under disability, this Rule applies"

-- Rule 13(2): "Subject to this Rule and to Order 11, Rule 7(c), the document must be served (a) in the case of a minor who is not also a person lacking capacity, on his or her father or guardian or, if he or she has no father or
-- guardian, on the person with whom he or she resides or in whose care he or she is; and (b) in the case of a person lacking capacity, on the person (if any) who is authorised under the Act to conduct in the name of the
-- person lacking capacity or on his or her behalf the proceedings in connection with which the document is to be served or, if there is no person so authorised, on the person with whom he or she resides or in whose care he
-- or she is, and must be served in the manner required by these Rules with respect to the document in question."
DECLARE `o 44 r 13(2) whom the document is served on` IS ONE OF
    `o 44 r 13(2) the father or guardian`
    `o 44 r 13(2) the person with whom the person under disability resides or in whose care the person is`
    `o 44 r 13(2) the person authorised under the Act`
    `o 44 r 13(2) someone else`

-- FORK QB | bare "must be served": served on someone other than the person the Rule names, or not in the manner these Rules require | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- FORK QD | the Rule does not apply (paragraph (1)): NOTHING, with `o 44 r 13(1) this Rule applies` answering JUST FALSE | JUST TRUE
-- src:6061 | 13. —(1) Where in any proceedings a document is required to be served personally on any person and that person is a person under disability, this Rule applies. (2) Subject to this Rule and to Order 11, Rule 7( c ), the document must be served — ( a )
-- src:6062 | in the case of a minor who is not also a person lacking capacity, on his or her father or guardian or, if he or she has no father or guardian, on the person with whom he or she resides or in whose care he or she is; and
-- src:6063 | ( b )
-- src:6064 | in the case of a person lacking capacity, on the person (if any) who is authorised under the Act to conduct in the name of the person lacking capacity or on his or her behalf the proceedings in connection with which the document is to be served or, if there is no person so authorised, on the person with whom he or she resides or in whose care he or she is,
-- src:6065 | and must be served in the manner required by these Rules with respect to the document in question.
@ref O 44 r 13(2) (src:6061-6065)
GIVEN `this Rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `o 11 r 7(c) Order 11, Rule 7(c) otherwise provides` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person under disability is a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person under disability is a person lacking capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minor has a father or guardian` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a person authorised under the Act to conduct the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      served IS A `o 44 r 13(2) whom the document is served on`
      `the document is served in the manner required by these Rules with respect to it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 13(2) the document is served on the person the Rule names` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `this Rule applies`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where in any proceedings a document is required to be served personally on any person and that person is a person under disability" -- the Rule does not apply (QD); `o 44 r 13(1) this Rule applies` answers JUST FALSE
           IF `o 11 r 7(c) Order 11, Rule 7(c) otherwise provides`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to this Rule and to Order 11, Rule 7(c)"
           IF (NOT `the document is served in the manner required by these Rules with respect to it`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); paragraph (2) does not say what follows when the manner is not as these Rules require
           IF `the person under disability is a person lacking capacity` AND `there is a person authorised under the Act to conduct the proceedings` AND served EQUALS `o 44 r 13(2) the person authorised under the Act`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the person under disability is a person lacking capacity` AND (NOT `there is a person authorised under the Act to conduct the proceedings`) AND served EQUALS `o 44 r 13(2) the person with whom the person under disability resides or in whose care the person is`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the person under disability is a minor` AND (NOT `the person under disability is a person lacking capacity`) AND `the minor has a father or guardian` AND served EQUALS `o 44 r 13(2) the father or guardian`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the person under disability is a minor` AND (NOT `the person under disability is a person lacking capacity`) AND (NOT `the minor has a father or guardian`) AND served EQUALS `o 44 r 13(2) the person with whom the person under disability resides or in whose care the person is`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); paragraph (2) does not say what follows when the document is served on another person

-- Rule 13(3): "Despite anything in paragraph (2), the Court may order that a document which has been, or is to be, served on the person under disability or on a person other than a person mentioned in that
-- paragraph is deemed to be duly served on the person under disability."
-- src:6066 | (3) Despite anything in paragraph (2), the Court may order that a document which has been, or is to be, served on the person under disability or on a person other than a person mentioned in that paragraph is deemed to be duly served on the person under disability.
@ref O 44 r 13(3) (src:6066)
GIVEN `this Rule applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document has been or is to be served on the person under disability or on a person other than a person mentioned in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 13(3) the Court may order the document to be deemed duly served on the person under disability` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `this Rule applies`)
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph is part of the Rule that applies under paragraph (1)
           IF `the document has been or is to be served on the person under disability or on a person other than a person mentioned in paragraph (2)`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a document which has been, or is to be, served on the person under disability or on a person other than a person mentioned in that paragraph"

-- Rule 13(4): "Subject to paragraph (5), a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing any act, a summons for the committal of any person, and an order to attend court issued to any person,
-- must, if that person is a person under disability, be served personally on him or her unless the Court otherwise orders."
-- src:6067 | (4) Subject to paragraph (5), a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing any act, a summons for the committal of any person, and an order to attend court issued to any person, must, if that person is a person under disability, be served personally on him or her unless the Court otherwise orders.
@ref O 44 r 13(4) (src:6067)
GIVEN `the document is a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing, any act, a summons for the committal of any person, or an order to attend court issued to any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person is a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is not an order for production or inspection of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 13(4) the requirement of personal service of the document applies` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`the document is a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing, any act, a summons for the committal of any person, or an order to attend court issued to any person` AND `that person is a person under disability` AND `the document is not an order for production or inspection of documents`))
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subject to paragraph (5), a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing any act, a summons for the committal of any person, and an order to attend court issued to any person, must, if that person is a person under disability, be served personally on him or her unless the Court otherwise orders" (the condition is not met)
           IF `the Court otherwise orders`
           THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless ... the Court otherwise orders"
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- FORK QB | bare "must" (Subject to paragraph (5), a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing any act, a summons for the committal of any person, and an order to attend court issued to any person, must, if that person is a person under disability, be served personally on him or her unless the Court otherwise orders): the requirement is not met | NOTHING | JUST FALSE for the compliance question
-- FORK QD | the duty does not arise (the "where", "before" or "unless" is unmet): NOTHING, with the companion `o 44 r 13(4) the requirement of personal service of the document applies` answering JUST FALSE | JUST TRUE ("nothing is unmet")
-- src:6067 | (4) Subject to paragraph (5), a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing any act, a summons for the committal of any person, and an order to attend court issued to any person, must, if that person is a person under disability, be served personally on him or her unless the Court otherwise orders.
@ref O 44 r 13(4) (src:6067)
GIVEN `the document is a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing, any act, a summons for the committal of any person, or an order to attend court issued to any person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person is a person under disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is not an order for production or inspection of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise orders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is served personally on that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 13(4) the document is served personally as the Rule requires` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT (`the document is a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing, any act, a summons for the committal of any person, or an order to attend court issued to any person` AND `that person is a person under disability` AND `the document is not an order for production or inspection of documents`))
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraph (5), a judgment or order requiring a person to do, or refrain from doing any act, a summons for the committal of any person, and an order to attend court issued to any person, must, if that person is a person under disability, be served personally on him or her unless the Court otherwise orders" -- the duty does not arise (QD); `o 44 r 13(4) the requirement of personal service of the document applies` answers JUST FALSE
           IF `the Court otherwise orders`
           THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless ... the Court otherwise orders" -- the requirement does not apply (QD); `o 44 r 13(4) the requirement of personal service of the document applies` answers JUST FALSE
           IF `the document is served personally on that person`
           THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must" (QB); O 44 r 13(4) does not say what follows when a requirement is not met


-- Rule 13(5): "Paragraph (4) does not apply to an order for production or inspection of documents."
-- src:6068 | (5) Paragraph (4) does not apply to an order for production or inspection of documents.
@ref O 44 r 13(5) (src:6068)
GIVEN `the document is an order for production or inspection of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 44 r 13(5) paragraph (4) applies to the document` MEANS
    IF `the document is an order for production or inspection of documents`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Paragraph (4) does not apply to an order for production or inspection of documents"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (5) speaks only of an order for production or inspection of documents
